# indent — real-world examples

## K&R style, no tabs, 3-space indents, wrap at 120 characters

```sh
indent -i3 -kr -nut -l120 main.c
```

## GNU style (the default)

```sh
indent -gnu main.c
```

## Linux kernel style (tabs, 8-wide)

```sh
indent -linux driver.c
```

## Homelab: reformat every C file in a project, keeping backups

```sh
# indent writes <file>~ backups automatically
find ~/src/homelab-tools -name '*.c' -exec indent -kr -i4 -nut {} \;
```

## Homelab: install on Tumbleweed

```sh
sudo zypper install indent
```

| Flag   | What it does                        |
| ------ | ----------------------------------- |
| -kr    | Kernighan & Ritchie style           |
| -gnu   | GNU coding style                    |
| -linux | Linux kernel coding style           |
| -i<n>  | indent size of n spaces             |
| -nut   | no tabs — use spaces                |
| -l<n>  | wrap lines longer than n characters |
